@--- Aug 15 2000 ---

I have a list of changes to make.

I have run a small survey (19 responses) which suggests that people do
not want multiple, named backups of games but would be content with a
single backup, and with some degree of autosave.  There are also
enough people interested in a smaller font and in rogue-relative
navigation that I feel justified in implementing them.

Here are the things to do, in order of attack

- Small font
  same basic issues as iLarn, except no town level
  remember the preferred font and switch to it when the app is launched
  make conditional compilation
  ...Ok, small font appears to be working.
- Rogue-relative movement
  remember or calculate the position on the screen of the rogue
  some tweaky testing will be needed to get it right
  run/walk will still be donutlike (if search is set to 10, it's ok.)
  ...Ok, ready to roll out (except as noted below in "minor bugs".)
  ...in random-letter==b, I also fixed the "hw scroll lists" request.
- Saving
  add a 'date of birth' to all save "files" to uniquely id the game
  add a timestamp to all save "files"
  have at least 1 slot for a snapshot, and allow an n-character comment
  have 1 slot for an autosave, and autosave when you go up/down stairs
  when you enter the app, check DoB and timestamp on autosave file, do popup
  at any time, allow (penalized) restore from snapshot or autosave, any DoB
  ... Ok autosave works, save and restore seem to work also
  ... oh yea vampirism works but hunger needs fine-tuning
  ... in random-letter==c, I also disabled 'drop' button when impossible.
  ... Should I include support for "multiuser" usage?
      I think I should just comment it out and ask if anyone actually
      uses it that way (it doesn't seem likely.)

minor bugs:
This was true before I tinkered with small font:
if you have 'centered' on, and walk e.g. one step north, then one step south
(also works with east/west) the screen slides the OTHER direction at first.
There must be something wacky in calculating where the center tile is?

--- June 26 2000 ---

0.40 has some bugs

- Fix it so that healing potions work better
  Ok - I revised the calculation (multiply by reasonable number, avoid Floats)
- Score is screwed up
  Ok - I revised the calculation (again, avoid Floats)
- Fix the top ten list to allow multiple entries per player
  Ok - done
- Don't record wizard scores (and warn each time a new character wizardizes)
  Ok - done

I might as well update some info strings also.
@


